333
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,020
And here's how to work out your own number

334
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:38,450
in about thirty seconds.

335
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,460
Write down what you'd want to spend a year

336
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:42,060
in retirement, in today's money.

337
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,810
Take off the state pension,

338
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:44,840
about

339
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:46,320
£12,548.

340
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,890
Then multiply what's left by 25.

341
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:51,530
That's the 4% rule turned around,

342
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:53,430
and it gives you a rough target pot.

343
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,640
Add a bit for tax, and remember that if

344
00:11:55,660 --> 00:11:57,700
you'll still be renting, rent goes in the

345
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,520
spending.

346
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:00,500
And when you get there, there are two main

347
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:02,530
ways to turn a pot into an income.

348
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,700
You can buy an annuity, which pays you a

349
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,160
guaranteed amount for the rest of your

350
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:08,630
life. Or you can use drawdown,

351
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:10,220
where the money stays invested and you

