353
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:13,410
Many people end up mixing the two.

354
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:16,000
It's worth getting proper guidance at that

355
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:18,120
point; the government's free Pension Wise

356
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:20,020
service is there for exactly that,

357
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:20,930
from age 50.

358
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:24,300
So the honest answer is: it depends on one

359
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:26,290
thing most people never think about.

360
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:29,350
Not your salary, not the stock market.

361
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:31,220
What you'll actually spend when you stop

362
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:33,750
working. A moderate life needs about

363
00:12:34,510 --> 00:12:35,310
£630,000.

364
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:39,530
A comfortable one, about £1.05 million.

365
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,930
And if you own your home outright by then,

366
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,040
you need a lot less, because rent or a

367
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:45,840
mortgage is one of the biggest costs there

368
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:46,660
is.

369
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,730
Which means you get to choose.

370
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:50,270
And the earlier you choose,

371
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:51,410
